# Error Handling

- Use project exceptions from `app.exceptions`: `AstraException`, `ConfigurationError`, `InfluenceError`, `ExternalServiceError`. Raise them for config validation failures, mind load/save failures, and external service failures so callers can catch specific types.
- Prefer specific exception types; avoid bare `except:` or broad `except Exception:` unless you re-raise or handle appropriately.
- When re-raising, chain with `raise ... from e` so the cause is preserved.
- Log at an appropriate level before re-raising (e.g. `logger.exception` or `logger.error`).
